# Trivy ignore file — Squadron OSS dependency-scan gate.
#
# The Trivy fs vuln job (.github/workflows/security.yml) gates on HIGH,CRITICAL
# for Go module dependencies (it skips ui/, whose production deps are gated by
# `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high` against package-lock.json — CI's
# actual install path). Frontend dev/build-tooling advisories are surfaced
# non-gating in the Trivy SARIF upload to the Security tab.
#
# Every entry below is an ACCEPTED finding: reachability-cleared and fix-tracked.
# A NEW HIGH/CRITICAL Go CVE that is not listed here turns the gate RED.
# Do NOT add an entry without a justification + TODO.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# golang.org/x/mod — two HIGH advisories, fixed in v0.40.0.
#   govulncheck (the reachability gate) confirms x/mod is imported transitively
#   but NOT call-graph-reachable from Squadron code, so these are not exploitable
#   here. Accepted; bump opportunistically.
#   TODO(security): `go get golang.org/x/mod@v0.40.0` then remove these two lines.
#   Ref: docs/security-gates.md (trivy section).
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

